pr: n2
title: JVM: the newdisp dispatch port, diagnostics and parity
branch: pr/02-newdisp-port

# Sections N3 (log lines 100..134) + N4 (135..159), 60 commits.
# Groups are contiguous runs in original order except where a `# moved:` comment says otherwise.

= JVM: camelCase the Kotlin runtime; tidy interop names and spawn output
The Kotlin runtime uses camelCase names throughout; BootJavaInterop spells its
names out; a spawn failure is reported to the merged stream. Groundwork before
the dispatch port touches the same files.
- 842563809 JVM: spell out the names in BootJavaInterop
- fc3a9423a JVM: report a spawn failure to a merged stream
- 306a9a71b JVM: camelCase the Kotlin variables

= JVM: port the newdisp dispatch mechanism, and run nqp's own dispatchers
The dispatch model, record, registry, syscalls and the boot dispatchers, with
the Tracked REPR and t/jvm/11-dispatch.t; docs/jvm-dispatch.md describes it.
nqp's own dispatchers (src/core/dispatchers.nqp) run on it. The stage0 jars
are regenerated from this compiler (the later of the two regenerations is the
one that survives the squash, deliberately).
- 5893aeebf JVM: port the newdisp dispatch mechanism
- d94a608eb Bootstrap JVM backend
- a5223b99b JVM: run nqp's own dispatchers

= JVM: resumable binds, QAST::ParamTypeCheck, HLL-reported bind failures
A dispatch resumes when a bind check fails; the bind-will-resume-on-failure
syscall; recorded dispatches reported under NQP_DISPATCH_TRACE.
QAST::ParamTypeCheck compiles, the HLL reports a bind failure, a container a
parameter already bound is not re-vivified, and a capture's named arguments
are read by index.
- d2238f199 JVM: resume a dispatch when a bind check fails
- d09fa840b JVM: report recorded dispatches under NQP_DISPATCH_TRACE
- 4b9684f62 JVM: add the bind-will-resume-on-failure syscall
- efd6b5f8f JVM: compile QAST::ParamTypeCheck
- 6b7cdaf01 JVM: let the HLL report a bind failure
- fc686856e JVM: don't re-vivify a container a parameter already bound
- cc6759b0a JVM: read a capture's named arguments by index

= JVM: route call and callmethod through lang-call and lang-meth-call
Every call compiles as a lang-call dispatch and every method call as a
lang-meth-call dispatch, with the arguments those dispatchers expect. What
routing everything needed: the raw KnowHOW gets a find_method and every
knowhow method an STable, a tracked lookup guards its table as MoarVM does,
and the bindcomplete op exists.
# NET-ZERO: the NQP_JVM_LANG_CALL gate is introduced by the first two commits
# and removed by the last one (routing by default); one group, so it never appears.
- 75516997d JVM: compile a call as a lang-call dispatch, behind NQP_JVM_LANG_CALL
- 6e85b3d0f JVM: compile a method call as a lang-meth-call dispatch, same gate
- 0936cc0ea JVM: give lang-meth-call the arguments it expects
- a61412085 JVM: give the raw KnowHOW a find_method, and every knowhow method an STable
- e0c1e800c JVM: guard the table of a tracked lookup, as MoarVM does
- ef86b72e2 JVM: implement the bindcomplete op
- 52cde5811 JVM: route call and callmethod through lang-call by default

= JVM: explode flattening at the dispatch entry, and key programs by shape
Flattening is exploded once at the dispatch entry and dispatch programs are
keyed by argument shape; full routing survives the core setting compile.
- 1df03422a JVM: explode flattening at the dispatch entry, and key programs by shape
- 22ba60970 JVM: make full-routing survive the core setting compile

= JVM: uint parameter ops, hllize edges, NO_HINT for an uncomposed type
The uint parameter ops; a failed rethrow names what it got; the hllize family
passes st-less objects through and hllizes a type object to the target
language's foreign type; an uncomposed type's attribute hint answers NO_HINT.
# moved: 553eeb106 (P6Opaque.kt) and 1e0dfdac6 (Ops.kt) pulled ahead of
# 6b40a7332, 102f96d70, cef172cba, cc5611a56 -- those touch only dispatch/*,
# jast2bc/AutosplitMethodWriter.kt and the *ControlException/JavaCallinException
# files; disjoint.
- c98104675 JVM: uint parameter ops, and name what a failed rethrow got
- 4b2a6f1d2 JVM: let the hllize family pass st-less objects through
- 553eeb106 JVM: answer NO_HINT for an uncomposed type's attribute hint
- 1e0dfdac6 JVM: hllize a type object to the target language's foreign type

= JVM: allocation off the replay path; intern autosplit inference strings
- 6b40a7332 JVM: take allocation off the dispatch replay path
- 102f96d70 JVM: intern the autosplit type-inference strings

= JVM: make control exceptions stackless, with causes threaded through
- cef172cba JVM: make control exceptions stackless
- cc5611a56 JVM: thread causes through the stackless control exceptions

= keep
- 92bcc943a JVM: dispatch through an Object[] when a callsite outgrows MethodType

= JVM: integer atomics, code-ref source locations, sized-native semantics
The integer atomic ops and getlexref_u are registered; every code ref
carries its source location; sized native storage (P6int/P6num and the
native ref lexicals) has MoarVM's semantics.
- 465e6fe40 JVM: register the getlexref_u op
- d1b017c0f JVM: implement the integer atomic ops
- 8face622f JVM: give every code ref its source location
- 20cd97c87 JVM: give sized native storage its MoarVM semantics

# ---- N4 ----

= JVM: backtraces in declared-source coordinates, and clearer failures
A frame's invocation is noted while it is live; backtraces render in the
declared source's coordinates; lang-call says what it was given when it has
no language; a serialization failure identifies its closure; an escaped
continuation tells its story.
- b4066506c JVM: note a frame's invocation while it is live, not only on leave
- da01884be JVM: render backtraces in the declared source's coordinates
- 435da25c4 JVM: say what lang-call was given when it has no language
- 9227517c5 JVM: identify the closure a serialization failure is about
- 0052cfa73 JVM: make escaped continuations tell their story

= JVM: dispatch method calls on Java interop wrappers, typed marshalling
Marshalled interop arguments are cast to their real types and method calls
on Java interop wrappers dispatch; the interop classfile dump is back behind
an env var.
- 625065d68 JVM: revive the interop classfile dump behind an env var
- 1c8855d04 JVM: cast marshalled interop arguments to their real types
- 8ee42f485 JVM: dispatch method calls on Java interop wrappers

= JVM: mid-block #line, :m/:i:m regex literals, General_Category uniprops
- ddb00a38a JVM: honor #line directives that change mid-block
- 2ba40e60e JVM: support :m/:i:m literals in regex compilation
- 5c2656122 JVM: answer General_Category through the uniprop ops

= JVM: compile hot dispatch programs into MethodHandle chains
DispatchCompiler turns a hot dispatch program into a MethodHandle chain;
native calls run through the dispatcher path; flattened attributes resolve
through the named class handle.
- 357b6e7f6 JVM: resolve flattened attributes through the named class handle
- 0ed8cd6b9 JVM: compile hot dispatch programs into MethodHandle chains
- 34f902d40 JVM: run native calls through the dispatcher path

= JVM: persist nested comp-mode units in the enclosing jar
Nested comp-mode units get MoarVM's treatment and are persisted in the
enclosing jar, loaded back through LibraryLoader.
- 6e97927f2 JVM: give nested comp-mode units MoarVM's treatment
- 6c89b113b JVM: persist nested compilation units in the enclosing jar

= JVM: MoarVM parity edges in regexes, natives, bigints and exceptions
Regexes match Unicode the way MoarVM does; a native assign lowers to a bind
where the target is in reach; a sized native parameter is truncated where it
is fetched; a flattened P6bigint unboxes to a long only when it fits and is
read into an unsigned native by the unsigned rule; a payload belongs to its
exception, an arity failure is worded as MoarVM words it; nqp::captureinnerlex
exists. Serialization and Java-stack diagnostics are env-gated.
- 7ccc69a74 JVM: env-gated serialization and Java-stack diagnostics
- 2873d1bb2 JVM: lower a native assign to a bind where the target is in reach
- a818f5850 JVM: a flattened P6bigint unboxes to a long only when it fits
- 890643d3b JVM: match Unicode in regexes the way MoarVM does
- e19e2d43f JVM: truncate a sized native parameter where it is fetched
- 72c6c1400 JVM: a payload belongs to its exception, not to the thread
- 01da7a5b3 JVM: word an arity failure as MoarVM words it
- 25ba1ea74 JVM: read a bigint into an unsigned native by the unsigned rule
- 93ca8ae9d JVM: implement nqp::captureinnerlex
